content.text:
The docs don't have a dedicated section on breakpoints in plain CSS. They give you two things to combine:

- **Raw media queries:** `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx` (the breakpoints table under "Working mobile-first" and the `max-*` table) lists each breakpoint's equivalent, e.g. `@media (width >= 48rem)` for `md` and `@media (width < 48rem)` for `max-md`. You can write these in your own CSS and set the variable inside:
  ```css
  :root { --my-var: 1rem; }
  @media (width >= 48rem) { :root { --my-var: 2rem; } }
  ```
- **Theme variables:** the "Customizing your theme" section of the same file shows that breakpoints are `--breakpoint-*` theme variables (e.g. `--breakpoint-md`). Referencing them with `theme(--breakpoint-md)` inside a media query isn't documented in the docs. The repo's own stylesheet does it, though, e.g. `@media (width <= theme(--breakpoint-sm))` in `src/app/globals.css:125`.

If you'd rather stay in utilities, `md:[--my-var:2rem]` also works, using the responsive variants from the same page.

